      "id": 1,
      "text": "Windsor was founded in 1768 by the Colonial Assembly on Gray’s Landing and became the seat of Bertie County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windsor%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1991 Windsor entered the National Register and was designated a Civil War Discovery Trail landmark, preserving its original 100‑acre core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historicalbemarlehighway.com/windsor-north-carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Cashie River winds through Windsor, where the town and Roanoke Cashie River Center rent canoes and kayaks for calm water adventures.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windsor%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 2013 documentary, \"If You Build It,\" followed a Bertie County design‑based high school program that built Windsor’s only U.S. farmers‑market pavilion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windsor%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Tuscarora people historically lived here; today some remain in the village of Tandequemuc, now called Merry Hill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windsor%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Windsor offers Livermon Park Mini Zoo and the Cashie Wetlands Walk, a nature boardwalk through untouched wetlands east of downtown.",
